      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path",
      "impact_statement": "crypto/x509's chain verification with untrusted intermediates runs when a Go program verifies a peer's certificate as a TLS client. Caddy in this image never does: deploy/Caddyfile sets auto_https off (no ACME), serves its own certificate from /data/certs, and proxies to plain-http upstreams on localhost (reverse_proxy to the Flask backend and the central server); it verifies no certificate. Fixed upstream in Go 1.26.10 / 1.27.3, which the Caddy build moves to once those are a week old.",
      "status_notes": "Decided by maintainer."
    },
