      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path",
      "impact_statement": "The system Python 3.9 (python3, python3-libs) is never executed in the image: the application, pip and the entrypoint run the base's Python 3.14 (/opt/app-root/bin/python -> /usr/bin/python3.14, which is also what `python3` on PATH resolves to), no package in the image requires python(abi) 3.9, and dnf - whose runtime it is - does not run at runtime. The flaw is in 3.9's ssl module (a server-side SSLContext freed while its sni_callback switches contexts), which no process loads. The fixed RPM (3.9.25-7.el9_8.6, RHSA-2026:89742) is applied once seven days public.",
      "status_notes": "Decided by maintainer."
